#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:7
#: 64979d6b359143a79ecf0072dfd1d1d5
msgid "Sensor Position Offset Compensation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:9
#: 17e4834393a24413b299ce77383459bd
msgid "ArduPilot includes compensation for sensor placement on the vehicle.  This page clarifies what parameters can be set and how they should be set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:13
#: 95fb62322f644a92a4f5ded03216cf52
msgid "In most vehicles which have all their sensors (IMU, GPS, optical flow, etc) within 15cm of each other, it is unlikely that providing the offsets will provide a noticeable performance improvement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:17
#: 9ad03db04b3d4026801f24d514703208
msgid "The sensor's position offsets are specified as 3 values (X, Y and Z) which are distances in meters from the IMU (which can be assumed to be in the middle of the autopilot board) or the vehicle's center of gravity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:19
#: ddd5d4f0aade4eecb7c4aac551ea6a86
msgid "X : distance forward of the IMU or center of gravity.  Positive values are towards the front of the vehicle, negative values are towards the back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:20
#: 3806b6ea95884de291c34217d8c47f08
msgid "Y : distance to the right of the IMU or center of gravity.  Positive values are towards the right side of the vehicle, negative values are towards the left."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:21
#: 7eb53d0219b74d82b292265c45322493
msgid "Z : distance *below* the IMU or center of gravity.  Positive values are *lower*, negative values are *higher*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:23
#: ba3acd6775b1451c9a16fb4b27a6948e
msgid "In practice the distance to the sensor can be measured from the center of the autopilot unless the autopilot itself is placed a significant distance from the vehicle's center of gravity in which case the IMU position offsets can be specified and then the other sensor's position offsets can be specified from the vehicle's center of gravity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:27
#: c4aea3033e9f4c8cabafd8d5ff9a3ff0
msgid "Parameter Details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:29
#: 0ebf848b1efd4d01b1d480386572dbb8
msgid "**IMU (aka INS):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:31
#: 6cc53966d8b047ce82490b50bc08c7b0
msgid "For the best results the autopilot (and thus the IMUs) should be placed at the center-of-gravity of the vehicle but if this is physically impossible the offset can be partially compensated for by setting the following parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:33
#: eca4c4e99d1e4f5b9e0a54df73daec3c
msgid ":ref:`INS_POS1_X <INS_POS1_X>`, :ref:`INS_POS1_Y <INS_POS1_Y>`, :ref:`INS_POS1_Z <INS_POS1_Z>` the first IMU's position from the vehicle's center-of-gravity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:34
#: c5f38a165c4e453595317d0eaa8c4127
msgid ":ref:`INS_POS2_X <INS_POS2_X>`, :ref:`INS_POS2_Y <INS_POS2_Y>`, :ref:`INS_POS2_Z <INS_POS2_Z>` the second IMU's position from the vehicle's center-of-gravity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:35
#: c07cf5276f9f46de9b5a232534228987
msgid ":ref:`INS_POS3_X <INS_POS3_X>`, :ref:`INS_POS3_Y <INS_POS3_Y>`, :ref:`INS_POS3_Z <INS_POS3_Z>` the third IMU's position from the vehicle's center-of-gravity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:37
#: 949ab6c1609a47029901c320fa220a9b
msgid "The compensation is only *partial* because ArduPilot can correct the vehicle's velocity and position estimate but it does not correct the acceleration estimate. For example if the autopilot was placed on the nose of a vehicle and the vehicle suddenly leans back (i.e. rotates so that its nose points up) with no offset compensation the vehicle velocity estimate would momentarily show the vehicle is climbing when it's not.  With the position offsets added the velocity would not show this momentary climb.  The EKF would still show a momentary vertical acceleration and because we use the acceleration in our altitude hold controllers this could still lead to the vehicle momentary reducing throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:42
#: 868bcf94771a4f33b5e5c5f292b1eb49
msgid "Although individual position offsets can be set for each IMU, the difference between the placement of IMUs on most autopilot boards is so small that the same values can be used for all IMUs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:44
#: c53fbcc32daa4af9a8e78ef182316560
msgid "if the IMU offset is specified, then all the following offsets are relative to **Center of Gravity** rather than the IMU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:46
#: d6089a16bd07458995a9f0bcf39abca3
msgid "**GPS:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:48
#: da125591e8bf45dc81dec336a5cafe10
msgid ":ref:`GPS1_POS_X <GPS1_POS_X>`, :ref:`GPS1_POS_Y <GPS1_POS_Y>`, :ref:`GPS1_POS_Z <GPS1_POS_Z>` the first GPS's position from the vehicle's IMU or center-of-gravity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:49
#: 1ec723b840ba4d708c7d6cb17a920b90
msgid ":ref:`GPS2_POS_X <GPS2_POS_X>`, :ref:`GPS2_POS_Y <GPS2_POS_Y>`, :ref:`GPS2_POS_Z <GPS2_POS_Z>` the second GPS's position from the vehicle's IMU or center-of-gravity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:51
#: 363838a1b7ff4e8080e5c94fa27881fa
msgid "**Range Finder (Sonar or Lidar):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:53
#: bc5bcc4c36804d09bd9a4fff9b3bd441
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_POS_X <RNGFND1_POS_X>`, :ref:`RNGFND1_POS_Y <RNGFND1_POS_Y>`, :ref:`RNGFND1_POS_Z <RNGFND1_POS_Z>` the first RangeFinder's position from the vehicle's IMU or center of gravity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:54
#: c9fae8c039744b29979cc4dc278f105a
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND2_POS_X <RNGFND2_POS_X>`, :ref:`RNGFND2_POS_Y <RNGFND2_POS_Y>`, :ref:`RNGFND2_POS_Z <RNGFND2_POS_Z>` the second RangeFinder's position from the vehicle's IMU or center of gravity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:56
#: 2072de3f584c4a6abdf0db45a107810c
msgid "**Optical Flow:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:58
#: 02625006821344fe8d1fe881500a3c4f
msgid ":ref:`FLOW_POS_X <FLOW_POS_X>`, :ref:`FLOW_POS_Y <FLOW_POS_Y>`, :ref:`FLOW_POS_Z <FLOW_POS_Z>` distance from the IMU or center of gravity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:60
#: 935229c1feb54886b67bfabc805ae090
msgid "**Visual Odometry:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.rst:62
#: 06c947e9e78345399830c413e90eb193
msgid ":ref:`VISO_POS_X <VISO_POS_X>`, :ref:`VISO_POS_Y <VISO_POS_Y>`, :ref:`VISO_POS_Z <VISO_POS_Z>` distance from the IMU or center of gravity"
msgstr ""
